<div class="pane">
    <div class="toolkit-page-heading">
        <span class="toolkit-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ iconSvg|raw }}</span>
        <h2>Advanced</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="light">Empties the caches right away, even if automatic invalidation or Cloudflare purging is switched off. "Purge all caches" goes from the origin outwards: Craft first, so the <a href="{{ kvCacheUrl }}">KV cache</a> refills from fresh data, then the KV cache, then <a href="{{ cloudflareUrl }}">Cloudflare</a>. Purged before the KV cache, Cloudflare would refetch pages built from stale data.</p>

    <div id="purge-status" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Status: <strong>ready</strong></div>

    <div class="field">
        <button type="button" class="btn submit purge-btn" data-action="toolkit/purge/all" data-confirm="Clear Craft's caches, flush the KV cache and purge the whole Cloudflare zone?">Purge all caches</button>
    </div>

    <hr>

    <div class="field">
        <p><strong>Single layers</strong></p>
        <p class="light">"Craft caches" clears everything in Craft's Caches utility: data and GraphQL caches, compiled templates, asset indexes, CP resources and temp files.</p>
        <div class="buttons">
            <button type="button" class="btn purge-btn" data-action="toolkit/purge/craft" data-confirm="Clear all of Craft's caches?">Craft caches only</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn purge-btn" data-action="toolkit/kv-cache/flush-kv" data-confirm="Flush the whole KV cache?">KV cache only</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn purge-btn" data-action="toolkit/cloudflare/purge-everything" data-confirm="Purge the whole Cloudflare zone?">Cloudflare only</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
